<description>
Erase the control bars and tile each matched sprite toward its bar.

Input structure
- The background contains colored non-line sprites plus one-cell-thick control
  bars.
- A horizontal bar has the same column span as a sprite; a vertical bar has
  the same row span as a sprite.

Rule
- Remove every control bar.
- For each bar, find the nearest sprite aligned with the bar's span on the
  perpendicular axis.
- Repeat that sprite periodically from its original position toward the bar,
  clipping at the grid boundary and leaving sprite-background cells empty.

Key insight
- The bar is not copied itself; it gives the direction and terminal line for
  repeating the aligned sprite motif.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_along_path",
  "src": "colored non-line sprite s matched to a one-cell-thick control bar sharing s's row span or column span",
  "path": "straight cardinal path from s toward the matching bar: vertical for a horizontal bar with the same columns, horizontal for a vertical bar with the same rows; stop after the repeated sprite covers the bar line",
  "trajectory": "copy s every full sprite height/width along the path, clipping at grid edges and treating background cells inside s as transparent",
  "dst": "aligned control bar marking the terminal row or column",
  "transform": "erase the control bars; keep original sprites and all copied sprite pixels"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 17-24 rows x 17-24 cols, background 0
  sprite:
    count: 1-2, all identical within an example
    shape: 4x4 hollow rectangle (border filled, 2x2 interior is bg) [observed]
    color: single non-bg, non-1 color
    size: height > 1 and width > 1 (solver requires)
  bar:
    count: 2-5 total, 1-3 per sprite
    color: always 1
    thickness: 1 cell (horizontal bar has height 1, vertical has width 1)
    placement: always on grid edge (row 0, last row, col 0, or last col)
    span: exactly matches the sprite's col-span (horizontal bar) or row-span (vertical bar)
    matching: each bar matches exactly one sprite via span alignment; nearest unique on perpendicular axis
    direction: bar is strictly above/below/left/right of its matched sprite (not adjacent)
  tiling:
    tiles_per_bar: 2-5 (including original sprite position)
    gap: distance from sprite edge to bar >= 1 sprite dimension (so >=1 new copy)
    overlap: tile paths from different bars or sprites never overlap outside the original sprite bbox
  output:
    bars erased; sprite tiled periodically from original position toward each bar, clipping at grid boundary
    bg cells within sprite bbox stay bg (transparent paste)

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Choose grid H x W in [17, 24].
    2. Choose 1-2 sprites; pick a non-1 sprite color C and define a motif (e.g. 4x4 hollow rect).
    3. For each sprite, choose 1-3 bar directions from {up, down, left, right}.
    4. For each (sprite, direction), pick tile count T in [2, 5]. Compute bar position = sprite_edge + (T-1)*sprite_dim in that direction; bar must land on grid edge -- adjust grid size or sprite position to satisfy this.
    5. Place sprites and bars so that tile paths do not overlap across sprites. Easiest: ensure different sprites occupy non-overlapping row bands and column bands.
    6. Build input by placing sprites and bars on a bg grid; bars are color-1 lines on the grid edge with the sprite's perpendicular span.
    7. Verify: each bar matches exactly one sprite, bar on edge, no tile-path collisions outside original sprite.
```
